B = [
('Talavera Uriarte','Latin America','17th century-present','ceramics','In the style of Talavera Uriarte, thick glossy milk-white tin glaze over rounded, weighty, hand-made forms, painted freely by hand in cobalt blue with accents of yellow, green, orange, black and sometimes turquoise. Decoration is loose and generous, with flowers, vines, leaves, birds, rosettes and geometric borders in slightly raised shiny paint. Pinholes, pooled colour and small unevenness in the surface are kept as part of the charm. Repeated panels join into large blue and white patterns. Rustic, festive, colonial and clearly handmade.'),
('Hereke Imperial Carpet Factory','Middle East','19th century','textiles','In the style of Hereke Imperial Carpet Factory, exceptionally fine surfaces with very dense, minute detail and a glossy silk sheen. Composition is courtly and symmetrical, built around a central medallion with pointed arch shapes, tulips, carnations, curling serrated leaves and rosettes, plus touches of gold and silver shimmer. Colours are ivory, turquoise, rose, deep sapphire, emerald and ruby. Borders are narrow, multiple and perfectly even, with soft elegant curves. Imperial, lustrous, exquisite and delicate.'),
('Batik Danar Hadi','Southeast Asia','20th century-present','textiles','In the style of Batik Danar Hadi, hand-drawn wax-resist patterning in an earthy palette of soga brown, indigo blue, cream and black, with occasional red and gold. Motifs are classical and rhythmic, such as diagonal bands of interlocking S shapes, circles in a quatrefoil grid, scattered tiny flowers and winged cartouches, repeated across the whole surface. Fine dotted lines and slightly wavering white outlines show the hand of the maker, and thin crackle veins and tonal depth appear where the wax cracked. Courtly, refined and heritage-rich.'),
('Bat Trang Ceramic Kilns','Southeast Asia','Traditional-present','ceramics','In the style of Bat Trang Ceramic Kilns, soft crackled ivory and cream-white glaze with freely brushed cobalt blue painting, and sometimes brown, green and iron-brown tones. Decoration is flowing and relaxed, with lotus, chrysanthemum, bamboo, birds, dragons, wave scrolls and key-fret borders, either brushed in blue or incised into the material. Forms have thick walls, swelling shoulders and a slightly uneven hand-thrown quality. Gentle, rustic, subtle and unpretentious.'),
('New Zealand Maori Arts and Crafts Institute','Oceania','20th century-present','carving','In the style of New Zealand Maori Arts and Crafts Institute, dense ancestral carving where every surface is covered in deep curved relief. Spirals, interlocked fern-frond curves and notched ridges flow continuously over bold stylised figures with large heads, wide inlaid shell eyes and protruding tongues. Dark polished brown wood is accented with red ochre, white and black, and woven lattice in diagonal patterns fills the spaces between carved elements. Powerful, sculptural, rhythmic and full of flowing curves.'),
('Thonet','Europe','1850s-1930s','furniture','In the style of Thonet, solid wood steam-bent into continuous flowing curves, with slender round-section members forming loops, circles and S-scrolls. Structures are light, airy and sculptural, with delicate splayed supports joined by a ring brace, and surfaces of woven cane or pressed perforated wood. Finish is dark mahogany brown, walnut or ebonised black in satin lacquer, with visible screw heads and small metal collars at joints. Later work uses bent chrome tube with cane panels and black leather. Mass-produced, elegant, coffeehouse mood.'),
('Herman Miller','North America','1950s-60s','furniture','In the style of Herman Miller, American mid-century modern design with molded plywood and fibreglass in organic curves, perched on thin wire struts or splayed wooden dowel legs with metal cross braces. Colours are warm walnut, ash and rosewood veneer, black leather with plump cushioning, and bright pops of orange, mustard yellow, turquoise and white. Egg, kidney and bubble shapes, slatted surfaces, exposed joints and brass or chrome hardware. Playful, optimistic, sunlit and honestly constructed, with later graphite skeletal frames and mesh.'),
('Knoll','North America','1940s-60s','furniture','In the style of Knoll, high modernist design pared down to structure, with polished chrome-plated flat steel bars bent in precise arcs and thin black or tan leather slung or tufted on top, held by visible buttons and straps. Single pedestal forms in white with round white marble or laminate surfaces, bent wire grids, glass on chrome X-frames, and sculpted rosewood. Palette of white, black, chrome, cream and saturated primary wool tweed. Sharp crisp edges, mirror shine, minimal, architectural and corporate in elegance.'),
('Vitra','Europe','1990s-present','furniture','In the style of Vitra, contemporary gallery-quality design with sculptural moulded plastic in matte pastel and primary colours, thin steel rod supports or wooden dowel bases, and witty oversized forms. Curvy shapes are wrapped in felt, wool or leather, with black ash, oak veneer and white lacquer as calm counterpoints. Mid-century shapes are mixed with deconstructed, geometric, exhibition-like forms. Clean shadow lines, crisp Swiss and German precision, colourful and playful, shown against seamless white backdrops.'),
('Artek','Europe','1930s','furniture','In the style of Artek, Finnish modernist design in pale laminated birch, with a single bent L-shaped support that curls into a smooth scroll beneath the surface. Forms are simple, round and light, with lightly curved plywood, soft rounded edges and visible blond grain. Natural birch and white lacquer are lifted by colourful lacquered parts in red, yellow, blue and green, black linoleum and striped woven webbing or canvas. Warm, humane Scandinavian functionalism with a nordic apartment and school hall mood.'),
('Fritz Hansen','Europe','1950s','furniture','In the style of Fritz Hansen, Danish modern design with sculptural moulded laminated wood in curvy ant, butterfly or egg silhouettes, with a pinched waist and no visible join between parts. Slim chromed steel tube supports on three or four points or a spiderlike cast aluminium base, tight leather or tweed wool upholstery, and coloured lacquered veneer in black, white, lime green, deep red and warm walnut. Surfaces are glossy and smooth with generous softness. Elegant, airy, organic in flow and never fussy.'),
('Carl Hansen','Europe','1950s','furniture','In the style of Carl Hansen, Danish cabinetmaker craft in solid oak, teak and walnut with soaked, oiled or soaped finishes that show fine grain. Shapes include curved wishbone-like members with steam-bent Y-shaped rails, hand-woven natural paper cord, tapered rounded legs, floating sculptural arms and round-edged surfaces. Pegged joints and visible joinery are celebrated. Palette of honey, pale blond, soft brown and cream leather. Calm, tactile, handcrafted, minimalist Scandinavian warmth.'),
('IKEA','Europe','1990s-present','furniture','In the style of IKEA, democratic flat-pack Scandinavian design in pale birch, pine and white-painted board, with simple rectangular boxes, slim peg or tapered supports and rounded corners. Palette is white and light wood with bright cobalt blue and sunshine yellow, plus muted grey, sage and pastel accents in textiles with stripes and checks. Modular open cubbies and lightweight stackable shapes keep things practical. Bright, airy daylight, cosy rugs, houseplants and clutter-free surfaces, friendly and affordable.'),
('Cassina','Europe','1960s','furniture','In the style of Cassina, Italian luxury modernism with deep, plump, tufted leather in cognac, black and cream on thin chrome or lacquered steel frames. Sculptural wooden members with a ladder-like rhythm and pale rush, wide leather planes, tubular steel supports and low lacquered surfaces with reflective glass. Rich materials include walnut, rosewood, polished marble, burnished brass and saddle-stitched hide. Sharp proportions blend craftsmanship with industrial precision. Refined, architectural, masculine and expensive, with a penthouse mood.'),
('Kartell','Europe','1990s-present','furniture','In the style of Kartell, Italian injection-moulded plastic in glossy, translucent polycarbonate, crystal clear, smoky, ruby red, fluorescent orange, lime and acid pink. Silhouettes are sculptural and sometimes baroque, with transparent ghost-like forms, smooth seamless curves and light passing through the material. Bright jewel colours and high-gloss reflections dominate, with pleated or bulbous translucent shapes. Playful, fashionable, pop and kitsch with modern luxury, shown in gallery-white settings with reflective floors.'),
('Alessi','Europe','1980s-90s','homeware','In the style of Alessi, Italian postmodern design with mirror-polished stainless steel and bright resin accents in red, yellow, pink, blue and green. Forms are playful and anthropomorphic, built from rounded cones, spheres and cylinders on spidery legs, with cute faces, exaggerated protrusions and cheerful little figures. Witty, toy-like and sculptural, treating everyday objects as pop-art ornaments, with soft shadows and cheerful display.'),
('Memphis Group','Europe','1980s','furniture','In the style of Memphis Group, Italian postmodern design built from clashing geometric blocks, triangles, cylinders and zigzags. Cheeky laminate in bold squiggle, terrazzo and speckled confetti patterns in pink, teal, mustard yellow, sky blue, black and white. Asymmetrical, wobbly, totem-like stacking, tapered legs, dayglo plastic and glass with stripes and dots. Flat saturated colour planes with thick black outlines. Playful, irreverent, cartoonish, kitsch and joyful, with a loud 1980s mood.'),
('Fornasetti','Europe','1950s','homeware','In the style of Fornasetti, glossy lacquered surfaces covered in printed black and white engravings with surreal repeating motifs such as a woman face with half-closed eyes, sun faces, playing cards, butterflies, keys, hands, architectural arches and classical ruins. Deep black, cream, bold red and gold accents with gilded edges. Dense graphic linework and trompe-l oeil illusion are applied to any shape. Witty, theatrical, cultured, ornamental and mysterious.'),
('Venini','Europe','1930s-50s','glass','In the style of Venini, Venetian art glass with thin hand-blown walls and elegant organic, asymmetrical forms, smooth, rounded and softly irregular, with wavy edges like folded cloth. Colours are luminous amber, aquamarine, turquoise, lilac, milky white and rich red, with patchwork mosaic panels, bands of fused colour, delicate lattice threading and acid-etched matte surfaces. Light-catching, subtly imperfect, jewel-like and sculptural, in a mid-century Italian spirit.'),
('Barovier and Toso','Europe','1930s-60s','lighting','In the style of Barovier and Toso, Venetian hand-blown glass in lavish, light-filled forms, with delicate curved arms spreading from a central axis and bearing glass flowers, leaves and curling ribbons in clear crystal, rose pink, aqua and amber. Ornate scrolling branches and floral cups sit beside mid-century sculptural versions with cascading rods, tubes and ball drops in white and gold. Glossy, translucent, festive, ornate and glittering like a palace ballroom.'),
('Lalique','Europe','1920s','glass','In the style of Lalique, French Art Deco moulded glass in frosted opalescent and crystal clear, with relief decoration of flowers, birds, dragonflies, nude female figures, fish and leaping animals. Satin matte frosting contrasts with polished highlights, with pale ice-blue and amber tints, black enamel details and stylised geometric borders. Sinuous curves and a glowing crystal sparkle give a refined, elegant Parisian luxury.'),
('Daum','Europe','1900s','glass','In the style of Daum, French Art Nouveau layered glass, thick and soft, with acid-etched and wheel-carved decoration of thistles, poppies, irises, mountain landscapes and wintry scenes. Colours are mottled and graded from smoky orange to deep green, milky mist, powder blue and amber, with enamelled and gilded highlights. Naturalistic plant forms swell around bulbous bodies. Soft translucence, dreamy, rich, with a subdued glow like looking through frosted weather.'),
('Baccarat','Europe','19th century','glass','In the style of Baccarat, French lead crystal, clear and brilliant, with deep geometric diamond cuts, fluted columns, faceted forms and heavy bases. Cut hobnail diamonds and prismatic edges sparkle, tiered pendant drops hang from gilded bronze arms, and occasional bright red cut glass adds richness. Dazzling refraction and rainbow highlights under candlelight, formal, opulent and palatial in a Second Empire manner.'),
('Orrefors','Europe','1930s-50s','glass','In the style of Orrefors, Swedish art glass, thick, crystal-clear and heavy-walled, with deep engraved or wheel-cut scenes, ethereal trapped air bubbles and abstract wavy colour patterns inside the material. Forms are streamlined, tapering and smooth, in a cool transparent palette with accents of slate blue, smoky grey and soft green. Understated, refined, sculptural Scandinavian modernism, pure and sparkling in cold light.'),
('Kosta Boda','Europe','1980s-90s','glass','In the style of Kosta Boda, Swedish contemporary art glass, bold, colourful and hand-blown, with chunky abstract forms, bright stripes, spots and swirled colour layers, and cheerful faces, birds, fish and clowns. Thick transparent bodies in saturated magenta, cobalt, orange, emerald and cool teal, glossy smooth surfaces and organic asymmetrical silhouettes. Joyful, playful and sculptural, with light refracting through thick glass.'),
('Iittala','Europe','1950s','glass','In the style of Iittala, Finnish glass design with organic fluid forms, undulating leaf-like curves, free-form wavy edges like lake shores, simple cylinders with rings of bumps, and small bird shapes in colour. Palette of crystal clear, smoky grey, sea green, cobalt blue, burnt orange and ruby. Smooth, rounded, minimal and soft, with moulded ripples evoking ice, water and birch bark. Nordic calm and functional beauty.'),
('Arabia','Europe','1950s-70s','ceramics','In the style of Arabia, Finnish stoneware and porcelain with simple rounded cylindrical and bowl shapes, stackable, with sturdy loop forms. Glazes in cream white, matte brown, ochre, forest green, mustard and speckled grey, or bright flat 1970s orange, yellow and brown abstract flowers and mushrooms in bold stencil and stripe patterns. Chunky, warm, earthy, practical and plain, with hand-painted irregularity and a cosy Nordic feel.'),
('Royal Copenhagen','Europe','18th century-present','ceramics','In the style of Royal Copenhagen, thin translucent white porcelain with hand-painted cobalt blue patterns, small blue flowers, ribbed fluted edges and delicate lace-like pierced rims. Brushwork is crisp, symmetrical and orderly, sometimes softened with pastel overglaze, and three small wavy lines recur as a quiet signature. Heirloom elegance, precise and serene, with an orderly rhythm of repeated motifs and a cool, clean blue and white palette throughout.'),
('Bing and Grondahl','Europe','1890s-1950s','ceramics','In the style of Bing and Grondahl, Danish thin white porcelain in soft blue-grey and white, with naturalistic Art Nouveau brushwork of seabirds, herons, stylised flowers and tall reeds in shaded cobalt. Muted pastel greys, creams, sea blues and lilac, smooth curved forms, delicate relief moulding with winter village scenes, and crackled and sculpted surfaces. Delicate, serene and quietly poetic.'),
('Wedgwood','Europe','18th century','ceramics','In the style of Wedgwood, matte unglazed stoneware in pale powder blue, sage green, lilac, black and cream, decorated with crisp white relief figures from classical Greek and Roman scenes, garlands, putti and acanthus borders. Fine sharp applied moulding sits on a smooth chalky background, alongside creamy glazed surfaces. Neoclassical symmetry, elegant, delicate and drawing-room refined, with a pale, powdery finish and fine, even detail across every surface.'),
('Spode','Europe','19th century','ceramics','In the style of Spode, English transfer-printed pottery with dense blue-and-white printing of classical landscapes with ruins, bridges, towers and trees, framed by borders of flowers and shell-like motifs. Cream-white ground carries intricately engraved line shading in deep indigo blue, and the same approach appears in Chinese-style willow scenes, floral chintz and red or green variants. Charming, traditional, old-world and cottage-like.'),
('Royal Doulton','Europe','1900s-1930s','ceramics','In the style of Royal Doulton, English ceramics ranging from stoneware with Art Nouveau tube-lined flowers in earthy brown, blue and green, to mottled red-and-black flambe glaze with running streaks, and hand-painted figures in crinoline gowns with grinning caricature faces. Glossy, richly coloured and finely detailed with pastel flesh tones, floral garlands, gilded edges and sculpted ruffles. Sentimental Victorian and Edwardian parlour feel.'),
('Newport Pottery','Europe','1930s','ceramics','In the style of Newport Pottery, English Art Deco design hand-painted with bold geometric zigzags, triangles, diamonds, stylised trees, houses and flowers in bright enamel orange, yellow, red, green, blue and purple, with black outlines on a creamy ground. Angular conical shapes, triangular details, stepped forms and cubist curves. Cheerful, vivid, jazzy, gloriously flat and modernist 1930s, with flat colour and strong outlines throughout.'),
('Meissen','Europe','18th century','ceramics','In the style of Meissen, lustrous white hard-paste porcelain with exquisitely hand-painted scattered flowers, vividly coloured birds and chinoiserie scenes. Rococo shapes, gilded scrolling borders, applied sculpted flowers and delicate lace-draped figures with pink cheeks, dainty gestures and pastel costumes. Blue and iron red onion patterns, luxurious, fragile, baroque palace showpiece, with a smooth glassy finish and playful, graceful detail throughout.'),
('Sevres','Europe','18th century','ceramics','In the style of Sevres, French porcelain with intensely coloured ground glazes in deep royal blue, turquoise, apple green and rose pink, framed by gold gilding and reserved panels painted with birds, flowers, pastoral lovers and cherubs. Rococo shapes with scrolled forms and ormolu mounts, and white unglazed biscuit figures. Opulent, ornate, gleaming gold, refined courtly taste, with smooth glassy finish and rich colour set off by crisp gilded edging.'),
('Royal Worcester','Europe','19th century','ceramics','In the style of Royal Worcester, English porcelain with hand-painted naturalistic subjects such as fruit, fallen blossoms, game birds, highland cattle and landscapes on an ivory ground, framed by raised gilding, jewelled enamel dots and pierced reticulated edges. Rich cream and blush ivory glaze, gold scrolling, oriental-inspired shapes, shell forms, twisting branch curves and delicate floral sprays. Finely detailed Victorian elegance.'),
('Haviland Limoges','Europe','19th century','ceramics','In the style of Haviland Limoges, French white hard-paste porcelain with delicate hand-painted pastel roses, violets and wildflower sprays, pale pink, mint and lavender scalloped edges with gold rims, and moulded basketweave and lace patterns. Thin, translucent bright white body, soft floral garlands, rounded forms with curled details. Light, romantic, feminine, cottage garden and Belle Epoque in charm, with a smooth, glassy finish and a gentle, fresh colour palette throughout.'),
('De Porceleyne Fles','Europe','17th century-present','ceramics','In the style of De Porceleyne Fles, Dutch tin-glazed earthenware painted by hand in rich cobalt blue on glossy white, depicting windmills, canals, sailing ships, tulips, milkmaids, farmhouses and floral scrolls, with fine brushwork and blue shading. Tiered, pyramid-like forms appear in some work. Slightly crackled glaze, soft blue-white contrast, charming, folksy Dutch heritage with elegant Chinese-inspired scenes, crisp and tidy in finish, nostalgic and gentle in mood.'),
('Faberge','Russia and Eastern Europe','1890s-1910s','decorative arts','In the style of Faberge, Imperial Russian jewelled preciousness, especially egg-like forms in layered translucent guilloche enamel in pastel pink, powder blue, mint green, lilac and cream over engraved sunburst patterns, framed by gold, pearls, diamonds and rubies. Miniature hidden surprises, hardstone carving in jade, agate and rock crystal, and delicate gilded neoclassical garlands, bows and laurel wreaths. Opulent, exact, royal treasury glitter.'),
('Tiffany and Co','North America','19th-20th century','silverware','In the style of Tiffany and Co, polished prestige in sterling silver and platinum, paired with a signature robin-egg pale turquoise blue and white satin finish. Bold chased patterns, engraved leaf and shell borders, repousse flowers and hammered Japanese-influenced surfaces with mixed metals, plus clean, simple settings that present a single gem. Minimal sans-serif engraved lettering, bright white gleam, clean and exclusive.'),
('Tiffany Studios','North America','1900s','lighting','In the style of Tiffany Studios, American Art Nouveau stained glass built from hundreds of small leaded opalescent pieces in rich greens, ambers, deep blues, orange and red, shaped into dragonflies, wisteria, peonies, poppies, dogwood and geometric borders. Bronze forms cast as tree trunks, lily pads or twisting stems with dark green-brown patina, iridescent peacock blue and gold glass, glowing jewel-like light and lush naturalistic mood.'),
('Georg Jensen','Europe','1900s-1950s','silverware','In the style of Georg Jensen, Danish sterling silver in softly hammered, organic sculptural forms, with smooth rounded bulbous bodies and ornament of grape clusters, berries, blossoms and curling leaves, and later streamlined plain silver with sensuous curves. Fluid bulging shapes, dark ebony or ivory-coloured accents, openwork stems and cabochon stones. Gleaming matte silver, restrained, elegant and handcrafted Scandinavian luxury.'),
('Christofle','Europe','1920s-30s','silverware','In the style of Christofle, French silver plate with strong Art Deco geometry, smooth cylindrical and faceted shapes, classic beaded and ribbed edges and engraved monogram cartouches. Mirror-polished silver with ebony or wooden accents, thick fluting, banded edges and pared down lines. Crisp elegant reflections, luxurious white linen and crystal, and a grand ocean liner salon mood, with heavy, substantial weight and a simple, disciplined rhythm of repeated bands.'),
('Stickley','North America','1900s-10s','furniture','In the style of Stickley, American Arts and Crafts Mission design in solid quarter-sawn oak with visible straight grain and ray flecks, rectilinear boxy forms, vertical slats, flat panels, exposed mortise-and-tenon joinery with pegs and keys, and wide plank members. Dark fumed brown finish, hammered copper or iron hardware, thick leather or canvas, leaded glass. Honest, sturdy, handmade and simple, with a lodge-like craftsman mood.'),
('Gillows','Europe','18th-19th century','furniture','In the style of Gillows, English Georgian and Regency craft in rich figured mahogany, rosewood and satinwood with crisp neoclassical lines, reeded tapering supports, brass inlay, ebony stringing and ornate lion-paw feet. Leather-inlaid surfaces, sabre curves, brass fittings and deep polished red-brown glow. Formal symmetry, refined country house and gentlemen club interior, with restrained, confident, well-proportioned detail and a warm, deep gloss over every surface.'),
('Liberty','Europe','1890s-1900s','textiles','In the style of Liberty, English Aesthetic Movement and Arts and Crafts design, with fine cotton lawn and silk printed in small-scale floral patterns, paisley, peacock feathers, stylised tulips and Celtic knotwork in soft jewel colours of plum, teal, rose, olive, mustard and indigo. Oak with simple pewter and copper fittings with beaten decoration, and a Tudor-revival timber-framed mood. Delicate, artistic, bohemian and romantic.'),
('Morris and Co','Europe','1860s-1900s','textiles','In the style of Morris and Co, English Arts and Crafts pattern with dense, flat, intertwined foliage, acanthus leaves, pomegranates, willow boughs, honeysuckle, tulips and birds, repeating in rhythmic symmetrical trellises and curving vines. Muted natural dyes of indigo blue, madder red, moss green, russet, olive and ochre on cream. Woodblock-printed, tapestry and embroidery look, hand-drawn with a medieval flavour, restful and rich.'),
('Wiener Werkstatte','Europe','1900s-1920s','decorative arts','In the style of Wiener Werkstatte, Viennese Secession craft with geometric abstraction, strict grids of black and white squares, concentric circles, stylised roses, wavy lines and bold block-printed patterns in orange, coral, turquoise, black and gold. Pierced squares in metal, ebonised wood, enamel, elongated forms with grid-patterned surfaces, chequered bands and stylised flowers. Sophisticated, rhythmic, ornamental modernism with precise linear elegance.'),
('Bauhaus workshops','Europe','1920s','furniture','In the style of Bauhaus workshops, German functional modernism built from primary geometry, circles, squares and triangles, using tubular steel, chromed frames, black leather straps, flat plywood, bent wood and white-painted surfaces. Palette of primary red, yellow and blue with black, white and grey. Slim cantilevered lines, nickel, opal glass spheres, abstract woven grids and lowercase sans-serif lettering. Rational, austere and factory-ready elegance.'),
('Shaker workshops','North America','19th century','furniture','In the style of Shaker workshops, American utilitarian craft in pine, maple and cherry with plain, tapered, turned legs, ladder-like rhythm with woven tape, delicate swallowtail joints and plain painted finishes in barn red, mustard yellow, blue-green and milk-paint grey. Clean lines, no ornament, honest dovetails, spare, serene and tidy, with sunlight and handmade perfection, slender, carefully balanced proportions and a quiet, humble dignity in every joint.'),
('Heals','Europe','1900s-1930s','furniture','In the style of Heals, English Arts and Crafts and early modern design in plain, light limed oak and fumed oak, with simple rectilinear forms, square-section legs, chamfered edges, brass or iron hardware, cut-out hearts and slender tall proportions. Painted pastel finishes with delicate stencilled flowers, bold geometric printed linen and cotton in modern greens, oranges and inky blues. Tidy, sensible and cottage-modern.'),
('Habitat','Europe','1960s-70s','homeware','In the style of Habitat, British swinging-sixties high street design, simple and affordable, with cheerful bright striped and checked cotton, white and primary-coloured enamel, chunky pine, stackable wood, earthenware, white porcelain, wire, paper lanterns, rush matting and bright rugs. Colours are red, yellow, white, orange and natural pine. Casual, youthful, continental bistro spirit with plants, bare floors and plain white walls, sociable and unfussy.'),
('Ercol','Europe','1950s','furniture','In the style of Ercol, English post-war design in pale elm and beech, with slender spindles, sweeping hoops, curved arms, splayed tapering legs and simple bentwood construction. Light blond finishes and darker stained elm with visible swirling grain, round-cornered boxes with tapered feet, spoke-like rhythm. Warm rust, olive and mustard tweed tones. Warm, domestic and gentle, with a suburban 1950s feel.'),
('G-Plan','Europe','1950s-60s','furniture','In the style of G-Plan, British mid-century teak and afrormosia, low and sleek with tapered round legs, angular brass details and two-tone panels in white and black laminate. Sculptural shapes have slim wooden frames and chunky tweed cushioning in orange, mustard, olive and chocolate, with round-ended forms. Rich orange-brown oiled grain, with clean horizontal emphasis and slim tapering supports. Optimistic, comfortable and suburban 1960s.'),
('Parker Knoll','Europe','1930s-60s','furniture','In the style of Parker Knoll, British traditional comfort with deep padded cushioning, tall sloping forms with ears, shaped polished walnut or mahogany timber with turned fronts, and short curving legs. Upholstery in floral chintz, tapestry weave, brocade, mustard velvet or green moquette, with buttoned details and fringed or piped seams. Cosy, grandmotherly and comfortable, with mechanics hidden under a skirted base, like a traditional lounge by a gas fire.'),
('Hille','Europe','1960s-70s','furniture','In the style of Hille, British modernist moulded polypropylene, with one-piece seamless forms on four splayed legs in primary red, orange, white, black and lime, rounded rectangular profiles and gently flared edges. Plastic cubes, plain plywood and bent-ply surfaces, shiny high-impact polymer with a matte texture, simple geometry and mass-produced elegance. Pop, optimistic and space-age 1960s, with a friendly, bold, uncluttered look that suits mass production.'),
('Sanderson','Europe','1860s-1960s','textiles','In the style of Sanderson, English wallpaper and chintz fabrics with large-scale painterly blooms, cabbage roses, peonies, hydrangeas, hand-drawn trailing leaves, birds and berries, and printed willow patterns. Palette of soft pink, duck-egg blue, sage green, cream, mulberry and gold, in printed cotton, linen and embossed wall coverings, plus mid-century abstract botanical prints. Graceful, romantic and traditional English country house.'),
('Cole and Son','Europe','19th century-present','wallpaper','In the style of Cole and Son, English hand-block-printed wallpaper, dense and lavish, with chinoiserie pagodas and flowering branches, hand-drawn exotic birds, oversized banana leaves, monkeys, lush tropical foliage and woodland animals. Rich colours of petrol blue, emerald, burnt orange, coral and charcoal against metallic gold or silver grounds, flocked velvety textures, damask motifs and stripes. Theatrical, elegant and bold, floor to ceiling, luxurious.'),
('Le Creuset','Europe','1950s-present','homeware','In the style of Le Creuset, French enamelled cast iron, heavy, rounded and generous, with domed volumes, fat loop shapes, a thick rolled edge and a bulbous finial. Finished in high-gloss glazes of flame orange, deep red, Mediterranean blue, sunny yellow, forest green and cream, with matte black interior and a gradient volcanic orange. Warm, sturdy, rustic farmhouse glamour in matching shiny colours.'),
('Staub','Europe','1970s-present','homeware','In the style of Staub, French cast iron with matte black enamel interior and darkly glossy, speckled exterior in grenadine red, deep blue, graphite and basil green. Heavy rounded forms with textured domed tops crowned by a small brass or nickel animal-shaped finial, such as a cockerel, cat or pumpkin, and chunky vegetable shapes. Rustic, weighty, restaurant-grade and traditional French bistro.'),
('Denby','Europe','1960s-70s','ceramics','In the style of Denby, English stoneware in rich, earthy, drippy glazes, with chunky rounded forms, wax-resist patterns and tactile dark edges. Colours are deep brown, mustard, blue-green, olive, smoky grey-blue and cream, speckled and reactive with natural variation, in brown-and-cream swirled and pebble-textured designs. Heavy, hand-thrown look, warm, practical and rustic, with a retro 1970s feel, thick walls, soft rounded edges and a handmade, slightly uneven finish.'),
('Pyrex','North America','1950s-70s','homeware','In the style of Pyrex, American glass and opal milk glass, with rounded shapes that nest in sets, in sunny primary colours of red, yellow, green and blue, or printed with mid-century patterns such as barns, daisies, gooseberries, snowflakes and starbursts in turquoise, pink, avocado green, mustard and white. Clear glass paired with rolled edges. Cheerful, bright, nostalgic farmhouse kitchen and diner.'),
('Fiestaware','North America','1930s-50s','ceramics','In the style of Fiestaware, American Art Deco design in thick, glossy, solid-colour glazes of cobalt blue, vivid red-orange, yellow, light green, ivory and turquoise, with concentric ring-shaped ridges, round forms, banded edges, bulbous rounded bodies and sharp-edged rings. Colourful mix-and-match combinations against plain surroundings. Cheerful, durable and bold, with rounded, streamlined shapes, a shiny, smooth, uniform finish and a sunny, sociable, democratic spirit.'),
]
